 "finding": "An oracle told the exact reflectivity, the background motion, the shaking's realisation and both physical models, lacking only which is true and the receiver noise, is bounded exactly: its detection rate exceeds its false-alarm rate by 2 Phi(Delta / 2) - 1, and no method told less does better, whatever the ground's texture. Pulse by pulse on the real dwell the formula for Delta holds (0.993 +- 0.025 of it; 1.011 +- 0.030 with the background ten times larger, which cancels). At 30 dB per resolution cell, under Giza's regional microseisms the oracle's bound for the bench room is 1.8e-06: its imprint would have to grow 7.3e+05 times, 7.7e+03 after allowing the local level ten times the regional, site amplification three times and 10 dB more SNR; at the noisiest stations on Earth 1.3e-04 (1.0e+04 and 1.1e+02 times). What this argument does not exclude is strong nearby shaking known exactly, at the worst of four sampled sides, the scattered wave carried unattenuated across the scene: for truck over a bump 15 m away, all pass, at 72 Hz (surface_favourable) the oracle's bound reaches 1.00, so this argument no longer excludes 95% found at 5% false alarms (it would below 0.57 of that motion); 14 cases are not excluded after the allowances. A large upper bound shows only that this argument does not exclude detection, not that any detector achieves it; that would take an implemented detector succeeding on independent tests. Depth is carried by the mark's shape in this model: rooms 15 m down, small and spread, leave 71% of the mark of a room 30 m down unmatched (the bench room 15 m down, 78%), so telling those two depths apart takes only 1.4 times the signal that detecting either takes; the superposition of small rooms holds to 3.7%."
}